<h1><span lang="EN-GB">Interactive Cross Sections</span></h1>
<hr align="left" width="98.974%" size="6" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <i style="font-style:normal;"><span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Polylines &gt; Cross Sections &gt; Interactive</b></span></i><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Interactive Cross Section</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command produces single polylines using a line defined interactively using the mouse and the current view. In this method the cross section is cut in an arbitrary plane defined by two mouse hits. The plane is defined by the line connecting the two points selected and is projected along the view direction. You can use points from scan data and meshes only. All polylines created by this method will be placed in separate group.</span></p>
<p><span class="Command">Interactive Cross Sections</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command is grayed if there are no scan data or mesh selections or all selections are hidden. It works on wholly selected entities as well as on partial selections. In case of partial selection if one of the end points is out of the selected area, the polyline is generated only within the selection.&#160;</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">When this command is called the mouse pointer changes to <sup>+</sup>V.</span><span lang="EN-GB">&#160;</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB"><img src="processing_polylines_files/image030.gif" width="32px" height="32px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt="">&#160;&#160;&#160; Mouse pointer in</span> <span class="Mode">Interactive Cross Sections</span> <span lang="EN-GB">mode</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-GB">Click on the view to define the section start point. Hold down Ctrl key to draw cross section parallel to the viewport OX or OY axis. Click again to define the end point. A section is created by the intersection of the plane (containing the line), which is orthogonal to the current view. If you want to cancel, right click when you are about to pick the second reference point. While in this mode you can rotate the viewport using</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Shortcut">Shift + left mouse button</span></b><span lang="EN-GB">, pan using</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Shortcut">Shift + right mouse button</span></b><span lang="EN-GB">, and zoom using</span> <b style="font-weight:normal;"><span class="Shortcut">Shift + middle mouse button</span></b> <span lang="EN-GB">or the mouse wheel.</span></p>
<p class="Example" style="color:#008000; text-decoration:underline;"><a class="dropspot" href="javascript:kadovTextPopup(this)" id="a1" style="text-decoration:underline;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="color:#008000;"><font color="green">Example</font></span></a></p>
<div class="droptext" id="POPUP237937138" style="display:'none'; x-ss-type:dropdown;">
